diff --git a/docs/control-authentication.md b/docs/control-authentication.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..856c867
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/control-authentication.md
@@ -0,0 +1,5 @@
+# Native control authentication
+
+The optional loopback control server requires `LIGHTCRAFT_CONTROL_TOKEN` in both the desktop app and its CLI/MCP client. Use a private, randomly generated 32-byte token, encoded as exactly 64 hexadecimal characters. Keep it out of command lines, logs, source control and shared configuration. Missing or invalid credentials disable the listener. Headless operation does not require a token.
+
+External clients must send `{"id":0,"method":"auth","params":{"token":"<private token>"}}` as the first JSON line on every connection and reconnect, then read the successful `ok` response before sending commands. Authentication frames are limited to 4096 bytes and must complete within five seconds. The native clients perform this handshake automatically and reject non-loopback peers. Existing clients need this handshake before using a patched app.
